hat she is Sailor Moon. As Sailor Moon, Usagi must fight evils and enforce justice, in the name of the Moon and the mysterious Moon Princess.\nL61: She meets other girls destined to be Sailor Senshi (Sailor Scouts), and together, they fight the forces of evil! This new edition of Sailor Moon will feature: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes! This version of Sailor Moon will be completely true to original. Join us as Sailor Moon returns to the U.S. for the first time in years!\nL62: 【15†more details】\nL63: \nL64: 【16†Shop Retail Partners】\nL65: ## Most Recent Volume\nL66: \nL67: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL68: ### 【17†Volume 12】\nL69: \nL70: As Galaxia picks off one Sailor Guardian after another, even those of the outer planets, Usagi finds new companions to help her fight her most nefarious enemy yet. FINAL VOLUME! This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL71: \nL72: 【17†more details】\nL73: \nL74: 【18†Shop Retail Partners】\nL75: ## All Volumes\nL76: \nL77: 12 Volumes Available\nL78: \nL79: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL80: ### 【15†Volume 1】\nL81: Usagi Tsukino is a normal girl until she meets up with Luna, a talking cat, who tells her that she is Sailor Moon. As Sailor Moon, Usagi must fight evils and enforce justice, in the name of the Moon and the mysterious Moon Princess.\nL82: She meets other girls destined to be Sailor Senshi (Sailor Scouts), and together, they fight the forces of evil! This new edition of Sailor Moon will feature: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes! This version of Sailor Moon will be completely true to original. Join us as Sailor Moon returns to the U.S. for the first time in years!\nL83: 【16†Shop retail partners】\nL84: \nL85: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL86: ### 【19†Volume 2】\nL87: The mysterious Tuxedo Mask has revealed his identity, forcing Usagi to come to terms with her growing affections for the masked vigilante, all the while defending the people of Earth from renewed attacks by the sinister “enemy”. Everything threatens to overwhelm even Sailor Moon when suddenly a new Sailor Guardian appears.\nL88: Could this new Guardian be the Moon Princess the Sailor Guardians are sworn to protect? This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL89: 【20†Shop retail partners】\nL90: \nL91: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL92: ### 【21†Volume 3】\nL93: Tuxedo Mask gone bad?! As more of her closest allies fall under the power of the evil Queen Beryl, Usagi comes closer to discovering the truth behind her past. The stage is set for an all-out battle for the fate of Earth between the Sailor Guardians and the forces of evil. But when the dust settles, a little girl calling herself “Usagi” falls from the sky and right into the arms of Mamoru.\nL94: What is her connection to Sailor Moon and why does she want the Legendary Silver Crystal? This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL95: 【22†Shop retail partners】\nL96: \nL97: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL98: ### 【23†Volume 4】\nL99: A new group calling themselves Black Moon is after Usagi and the rest of the Sailor Guardians, wielding a new power known only as the Malefic Black Crystal. Chibi-Usa may be the key to it all, but to find the answers and rescue her kidnapped friends, Usagi will have to journey through time to the 30th century and discover what fate has in store.\nL100: This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL101: 【24†Shop retail partners】\nL102: \nL103: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL104: ### 【25†Volume 5】\nL105: Chibi-Usa gets sucked into the far reaches of space-time and vanishes! It’s up to Tuxedo Mask to reach her and get her back safely while Sailor Moon and the others must escape Nemesis and the evil clutches of Wiseman and his cronies.\nL106: But as Tuxedo Mask travels through the space-time storm, he encounters an ominous woman claiming to be his daughter! Who is this strange woman? Is she really Chibi-Usa?! This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL107: 【26†Shop retail partners】\nL108: \nL109: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL110: ### 【27†Volume 6】\nL111: Just when all seems well again in the world, another enemy appears! Two new figures from the private school, Mugen Academe, appear and take a special interest in Sailor Moon and company.\nL112: Who are they, and do they have anything to do with the strange occurrences that are suddenly taking place? Meanwhile, the appearance of two new Guardians takes everyone by surprise as our favorite Sailor heroes must once again face off against new enemies to save the world! This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL113: 【28†Shop retail partners】\nL114: \nL115: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL116: ### 【29†Volume 7】\nL117: Old friends and new enemies lurk in the mysteries surrounding Mugen Academe.\nL118: The Death Busters crave the Hoste, the human energies, of Sailor Moon and her friends —and they’ll prey on the girls’ dreams and weaknesses to get it! Furthermore, prophetic dreams hint of “talismans“ that could awaken a “Deity of Destruction.” Could these things be connected to the guardians’ power? And are the Sailor Senshi capable of murdering the innocent to save the entire world? This new edition of Sailor Moon features: An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! The original Japanese character names! Detailed translation notes!\nL119: 【30†Shop retail partners】\nL120: \nL121: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL122: ### 【31†Volume 8】\nL123: Chibi Usa’s sickly friend Hotaru isn’t just Sailor Saturn, Deity of Destruction. She’s also possessed by Master Pharaoh 90. Facing this cataclysmic power will be impossible —unless Sailor Moon can unite the powers of every Guardian of the Solar System. Then, when the moon eclipses the sun, a mystical unicorn begs for help.\nL124: An elaborate ship floats through the sky, and Usagi and Chibi-Usa have trouble seeing eye to eye… This new edition of Sailor Moon features: An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! The original Japanese character names!\nL125: 【32†Shop retail partners】\nL126: \nL127: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL128: ### 【33†Volume 9】\nL129: Amidst the chaos caused by Usagi and Chibi-Usa’s body swap, courtesy of the Amazoness PallaPalla, the Sailor Guardians’ primary concern remains Mamoru’s illness and its possible link to the newcomers in town, the Dead Moon Circus. The Amazonesses and their circus animal lackeys go after the guardians one by one, tempting them with false visions. However, each of the Sailors manage to defeat the enemy after their inner selves show them their individual heart crystals and new weapons.\nL130: Meanwhile, it is still a toss-up who the “young maiden“ is that Elysion priest Helios seeks: She who shall find and unlock the Golden Crystal that will save Earth, Elysion, and Mamoru! This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL131: 【34†Shop retail partners】\nL132: \nL133: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL134: ### 【35†Volume 10】\nL135: The threat of Dead Moon Circus is so great that the outer planet Guardians return to fight alongside their compatriots. But with Usagi now coughing up black blood as well, are they too late? And to make things worse, Queen Nehelenia’s servant Zirconia casts another curse upon Usagi and Mamoru, sending them both back into childhood. However, Helios whisks away their spirits to Elysion, where they manage to break free and return to their true forms.\nL136: After they rejoin their companions, the final showdown against Queen Nehelenia herself begins! Will the Sailor Guardians and Tuxedo Mask manage to save Earth and Elysion before the Queen transforms them into eternal realms of nightmares? This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL137: 【36†Shop retail partners】\nL138: \nL139: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL140: ### 【37†Volume 11】\nL141: \nL142: As life appears to return to normal for everyone else, Usagi’s turns upside-down in a mundane way with Mamoru leaving to study abroad for a year in America and Chibi-Usa returning to the thirtieth century. This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL143: \nL144: 【38†Shop retail partners】\nL145: Pretty Guardian Sailor Moon\nL146: ### 【17†Volume 12】\nL147: \nL148: As Galaxia picks off one Sailor Guardian after another, even those of the outer planets, Usagi finds new companions to help her fight her most nefarious enemy yet. FINAL VOLUME! This new edition of Sailor Moon features: - An entirely new, incredibly accurate translation! - Japanese-style, right-to-left reading! - New cover art never before seen in the U.S.! - The original Japanese character names! - Detailed translation notes!\nL149: \nL150: 【18†Shop retail partners】\nL151: ## A history of re-imagining the world\nL152: \nL153: For over a century, Kodansha has relentlessly pursued quality and creativity, which allows us to continuously reimagine what could be. We see the world without restrictions. A place of diverse passions, profound perspectives and limitless potential. Filled with curious minds and unexpected voices. And as we continue to shine a light on them, there is no telling how much further we can go.\nL154: ## Company\nL155: \nL156:   * 【39†About Kodansha】\nL157:   * 【40†→ Kodansha Corporate Site†www.kodansha.com】\nL158:   * 【41†→ Kodansha House†kodanshahouse.com】\nL159:   * 【42†→ K MANGA†kmanga.kodansha.com】\nL160: \nL161: ## Resources\nL162: \nL163:   * 【43†K MANGA Chapters】\nL164:   * 【44†Kodansha Reader Benefits】\nL165:   * 【45†Support Center】\nL166:   * 【46†Librarians & Educators】\nL167:   * 【47†Audio Resources】\nL168: ## RSS\nL169: \nL170:   * 【48†Release Calendar】\nL171: \nL172: 【49†We do not sell personal information】\nL173: \nL174:   * 【50†Copyrights】\nL17